        example: "enc.copy_buffer(&src, 0, &dst, 0, 64);\n\
            \n\
            main.vl:44:9: gpu.usage: copy_buffer's destination, its third argument (a buffer of 64 bytes), was made without BufferUsage::COPY_DST",
    },
    Explain {
        code: "gpu.entry",
        severity: "error",
        means: "(0.26.0) A field of an embedded block that is not one of its entry points: \
            `K.step` is the name of the `@compute`, `@vertex` or `@fragment fn step` of `embed \
            wgsl K { .. }`, for `compute_pipeline` and `render_pipeline`; the message lists \
            the block's entry points with their stages. A commented-out entry point is not \
            one.",
        fix: "Name one of the entry points the message lists (`volec fix --suggested` writes \
            the nearest), or add the entry point to the block.",
        example: "let pipe = dev.compute_pipeline(shader, SIM.stpe)?;\n\
            \n\
            main.vl:30:41: error[gpu.entry] the block 'SIM' has no entry point 'stpe'; its entry points: init (compute), step (compute)\n\
            \x20 help: did you mean 'step'?\n\
            \x20 try: volec fix --suggested main.vl",
    },
